# RangeCard 1.3 — design handoff

Implementation brief for the "fixes & a warmer feel" redesign. Written for
Claude Code (or a human) working in this repo.

```
design/handoff/
  README.md        ← this brief
  screens/         ← rendered target for every screen (390px wide, @2x)
  source/          ← design source per screen (HTML + inline SVG; copy exact
                     colours, spacing and SVG path data from here)
public/photos/     ← 7 royalty-free photos (Unsplash/Pexels), WebP, 18–140 KB
```

The `source/*.dc.html` files are design mockups, not app code. Read them for
values and SVG paths. Don't import them. Hard-coded hexes in them map to the
existing tokens in `app/globals.css` (dark block): `#0B0E18` = `--bg`,
`#161B29` = `--card`, `#1E2433` = `--inset`, `#222839` = `--hairline`,
`#2E3547` = `--border`, `#F2F5F9` = `--text`, `#C3CBD8` = `--text-2`,
`#9AA4B4` = `--muted`, `#96D6E2` = `--state` / `--ink`, `#E8938B` = `--clay`.
**Always use the tokens**, so light mode keeps working.

## Ground rules

- Change only what's listed. Keep all logic, data, IndexedDB schema and copy
  not mentioned here.
- Photos set the mood, drawings teach. Don't put photos on instruction
  screens (warm-up, routine, drill cards).
- Every photo header gets the same scrim, so text stays AA-legible in both
  themes:
  `linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(11 14 24 / .35) 0%, rgb(11 14 24 / .05) 30%, rgb(11 14 24 / .55) 70%, var(--bg) 100%)`
  Make it a reusable `<PhotoHeader src alt eyebrow title sub>` component.
- Photos must work offline: add `/photos/*.webp` to the service worker
  (`public/sw.js`) as cache-first, and precache them on `install`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; no new animations needed.
- After each phase: `npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build`, then check the screen
  in the browser at 390×844 against `screens/`.

---

## Phase 1 — bugs (do these first, one commit each)

### 1. Screens open part-way down
Switching tab/screen keeps the old scroll position, so the warm-up's first
exercise and the Log's first block open hidden under the sticky header.
Nothing in the app calls `scrollTo` today.
- `app/page.tsx`: add `useEffect(() => { window.scrollTo(0, 0); }, [tab]);`
  next to `const [tab, setTab] = useState<Tab>("home")` (~line 362). Also
  reset when a More sub-screen opens, if that's tracked in separate state.
- Check: Plan → Start session → warm-up shows "Shoulders" fully, under the
  header.

### 2. Floating nav covering the last item
`.app` has `padding-bottom: calc(96px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))`
(`app/globals.css` ~431). Scroll to the very bottom of Pre-shot routine,
Practice games, More and a Round hole. If the last control is still under
the nav pill, raise it to the pill's real height + 24px.
- Pre-shot routine: make "Rehearse it" (`components/Routine.tsx` ~83) a sticky
  bar that sits **above** the nav pill (see `screens/06-routine.jpg`).

### 3. Log title wraps to a lone "1"
`app/page.tsx` ~1440 renders `"Week 1 · Session 1"` in `.hdr-title.sm` beside
two buttons, so it wraps.
- Eyebrow: `Week 1 · Foundations` (replaces "Session log"). Title: `Session 1`.
  Add `white-space: nowrap` to the title.
- Target: `screens/04-log.jpg`.

### 4. Session receipt calls a good area weak
`components/SessionReceipt.tsx` ~45/150: `worst` is computed even when only
one area was logged, so 3/4 chipping (75%) shows "Chipping needs the attention".
- Only compute `worst` when `rows.length >= 2` **and** it is below 50%.
- With one area: show "Log a second area next time and I'll show you where to
  spend your balls."
- Lead the card with the best area ("BEST TODAY · CHIPPING · 75%").
- Target: `screens/05-session-done.jpg`.

### 5. Fixes contradicts the setup answer
Onboarding offers "Right, a slice: starts right or curves away late", but
`components/Fixes.tsx` `yourMiss()` maps it to the `slice` fault in
`lib/faults.ts`, whose `pattern` is "Starts left, curves hard right" (a
pull-slice).
- When `context === "From your setup answer"`, show the user's own words as
  the headline: eyebrow "YOU TOLD US", title "Starts right, or curves away
  late". Keep the fault's cause/fix body.
- Draw the matching ball-flight diagram (two flights right of a dashed target
  line); the SVG is in `source/Fixes.dc.html`.
- Target: `screens/09-fixes.jpg`.

